  "result": "{\"seen_before\": true, \"matches\": [\"PowerToys#43968\", \"PowerToys#46619\", \"PowerToys#37508\"], \"answer\": \"This has been reported before. Command Palette's Apps extension shows the Windows shortcut overlay arrow on app icons, because the icons come from .lnk Start Menu shortcuts. The earlier tickets, #43968 and #46619, ask for an option to remove or hide that overlay. #46619 was closed as a duplicate of #43968. I found no fix or setting in those tickets, so there is nothing to change on your side yet. Add your screenshots or a thumbs-up to #43968 to support the request. In #37508, a maintainer noted that the larger 'Jumbo' icons in Command Palette don't show the arrow, and that a similar helper could be added to PowerToys Run. That suggests the arrow could be removed in the same way.\"}",
